the battle to clear Isis from its last  stronghold in Syria entered a critical  new phase this morning for more than two  months Charlie d'Agata has been  reporting from the frontlines in eastern  Syria and that's where us-backed forces  are making what they hope to be the  final move against Isis Charlie went to  see the fight under cover of darkness  and he sent us this report from bagus  Syria where a shrinking group of Isis  fighters is trying to hold on  after weeks of fighting in what has  become a virtual stalemate we got word  this morning from the Syrian democratic  forces we can confirm they have entered  that last Isis camp but they cautioned  that fighting is still going on and  certainly as of last night the battle  was raging moonlight alone lit the way  as us back Syrian soldiers gave us a  close-up view of what's left of Isis  we're just on the edge of the front line  and these are sniper positions looking  down into the goose where Isis is  fighting back  sounds of both coalition fighter jets an  incoming gunfire filled the air we've  been told to stay low because just on  the other side of that Ridge is an Isis  position and as soon as we got here we  heard bullets whizzing overhead for  weeks American and coalition airstrikes  had pummeled a tiny slice of land not  more than a few hundred yards wide it's  hard to imagine how anybody can survive  yet by day they emerged to battle  America's allies on the ground here  soldiers of the Syrian democratic forces  some look like teenagers augury kobani  told us they were taking aim at a group  of Isis fighters trying to hide behind  trees are you surprised they're still  fighting it's still going on he said but  there's progress every day but progress  is slow and while the so-called  Caliphate is now little more than a  junkyard heaped with wrecked cars  hardcore Isis holdouts have managed to  defend it against every  in America and its allies have been able  to unleash for months now nobody here is  celebrating yet and there were  airstrikes over night we heard gun  battles this morning but the  announcement from the Syrian democratic  forces that their soldiers have now  entered that last Isis camp may be a  significant step forward for CBS this  morning Charlie d'Agata in bogus eastern  Syria we all hope that's true thank you  Charlie
 

